==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{m|ine-pro|*snewbʰo-||to marry, to wed}}. Possibly cognate with {{etyl|grc|-}} {{term|νύμφη||bride, young wife, nymph|lang=grc}} (English {{term|nymph|lang=en}}), but this is disputed.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈnuː.boː/|lang=la}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|nūbō|nūbere|nūpsī|nūptum|conj=3}}

# {{label|la|transitive|rare}} I [[cover]], [[veil]].
# {{label|la|intransitive|with dative}} I veil myself for, get married to, [[marry]], [[wed]] (for a woman).
## {{label|la|intransitive|of plants}} I become joined, tied or [[wedded]] (to).

